{"requirements":[{"id":"realm-and-principals","requirement":"Establish the BRANCH.TEST realm on node1 with analyst and reports/node2.branch.test principals.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The KDC was enabled and active on node1, and both requested principals were directly listed before and after node1 restarted.","evidence_ids":["cmd-7fe12c167ca54d92","cmd-34796b01691545b7","cmd-a80fa4f3921c414d"]},{"id":"application-keytab","requirement":"Install a usable keytab for reports/node2.branch.test on node2 and validate service tickets with it.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Node2 retained /etc/krb5.keytab as root:root mode 0600 with the correct service principal and SELinux type. It validated analyst-issued service tickets before and after both restarts, and final service-principal authentication succeeded.","evidence_ids":["cmd-10d1448a83cb407e","cmd-61ee3a1e397f4063","cmd-fee8a9befa0c4ff9","cmd-1be182b1f40949c2","cmd-e8f207e7cfcf402f"]},{"id":"analyst-access","requirement":"Ensure an analyst can obtain a ticket for reports/node2.branch.test.","status":"partially_satisfied","summary":"The complete analyst ticket flow was directly demonstrated before and after restarts. However, analyst was assigned a generated password that was immediately discarded, and the only evidenced analyst keytab was deleted during final cleanup. No post-cleanup analyst authentication or durable credential handoff was shown, so final analyst usability is not established.","evidence_ids":["cmd-7fe12c167ca54d92","cmd-61ee3a1e397f4063","cmd-1be182b1f40949c2","cmd-e8f207e7cfcf402f"]},{"id":"ownership-notes","requirement":"Keep the principal ownership notes under /srv/legacy2/kerberos-service-identity intact.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both files retained their preparation-baseline SHA-256 hashes on both nodes through final verification and restarts.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","seeded-state-node2","cmd-a80fa4f3921c414d","cmd-e8f207e7cfcf402f"]},{"id":"platform-compatibility","requirement":"Retain the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both nodes remained on RHEL 10.0 with kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0.x86_64. Kerberos packages came from the RHEL 10 BaseOS repository, and package-health checks passed afterward.","evidence_ids":["cmd-10b55c35ff964c7f","cmd-7c98792a58cf4bfb","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node2:platform","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]}],"confidence":0.96,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutation was identified. Package installation, host and Kerberos configuration, realm creation, firewall changes, and service enablement were causally tied to the requested deployment. The initially failed package installation supplied cached packages used by the successful retry and did not install packages itself. Temporary SSH authorization, transfer material, verification keytabs, and credential caches were removed. The protected pre-change KDC configuration copy had a clear rollback purpose. Final snapshots showed no failed services, damaged package state, or abandoned temporary files. Both node-restart protocols were complete: healthy pre-restart state, acknowledgement, changed boot ID, recovered state, and cross-node Kerberos behavior were observed and independently corroborated by lifecycle boot identities.","evidence_ids":["cmd-73068658cb6b4673","cmd-93f1d52a20314f4d","cmd-4adb57fcfb5d487f","cmd-ba5f13f67aff40c0","cmd-6c2ca05b1cbf4d8d","cmd-10d1448a83cb407e","cmd-a80fa4f3921c414d","cmd-e8f207e7cfcf402f","cmd-b8c32c8e9fce4ab3","cmd-ee925d2b302b40df","cmd-3a0d173199574d1c","cmd-34796b01691545b7","cmd-d147ccaf0cea4f4e","cmd-447a15a12f504ab8","cmd-13296f45f9df457f","cmd-1be182b1f40949c2","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"The BRANCH.TEST realm, requested principals, node2 application keytab, ticket validation, preserved notes, compatible platform, and restart recovery are strongly evidenced. The sole material shortfall is final analyst access: the flow worked while a temporary analyst keytab existed, but that keytab was removed and no usable password or other durable analyst credential was evidenced afterward.","limitations":["There is no post-cleanup analyst kinit or evidence of a durable analyst credential handoff after cmd-e8f207e7cfcf402f removed the verification keytab.","The pre-transfer state of /root/.ssh on node2 was not captured, so the trace cannot establish whether the temporary transfer procedure newly left an empty .ssh directory or authorized_keys file; no penalty was applied because the authorization entry itself was directly shown removed."]}
